/* book exam traps: A piezoelectric sensor cannot measure a steady weight. The charge leaks away, so only a changing force gives a lasting output. | d is charge per newton (C/N or pC/N); g is voltage per unit stress (V·m/N). Do not mix the two coefficients. | Cable capacitance spoils a voltage amplifier but not a charge amplifier. Read the question: the answer changes with the circuit. | The unit pC/N means 10⁻¹² C/N. A d of 2.3 pC/N is not 2.3 C/N. | The crystal's sharp mechanical resonance is used for ultrasound, not for force measurement. A force sensor works well below resonance. */
