/* book: lead: An ultrasonic sensor sends a burst of sound above human hearing and listens for the echo; the delay gives distance, level or flow. An acoustic sensor measures audible sound pressure. Both work without touching the target, so they suit parking aids, tank level, blood-flow probes, scanners and crack checks. */
/* book Figure 4.2.1: The pulse goes to the obstacle and back, so the 12 ms time of flight covers 2d and the obstacle is 2.058 m away. The 1.0 ms pulse length sets the range resolution of 0.17 m. */
